admin-role-purpose-super_admin = Full administration across every capability, including administrators, roles, security, mail routing and service configuration. Reserve this role for trusted operators responsible for the whole deployment.
admin-role-purpose-domain_admin = Day-to-day user and domain administration: create, update, disable or delete users; manage quotas, user capabilities, domain sign-in rules, settings and branding; revoke sessions and manage bans. It also includes mail diagnostics and usage/data exports. It does not grant administrator-role management or upstream-server changes.
admin-role-purpose-helpdesk = Account support and incident triage: inspect users, audit activity and usage; change user flags, disable accounts and revoke sessions; view bans and run sign-in simulations. It does not grant user creation, deletion, quota changes or general settings writes.
admin-role-purpose-auditor = Inspection and reporting: grants every capability ending in .read, plus audit and usage export. It does not grant configuration changes or account mutations. Exported reports may contain sensitive administrative information.
admin-role-purpose-security_officer = Security operations: manage security and MFA policies, sign-in policy and bans; disable users, revoke sessions or API keys; inspect and export audit activity; read authentication logs and run diagnostics. SSO configuration is readable, but this role does not grant SSO editing or administrator-role management.
admin-role-purpose-custom = A custom role with { $count } selected permissions. Its authority comes from the exact permission list below, not its name. Review each action before assigning it.
admin-role-purpose-scope = Domain scope is assigned when this role is granted to an administrator. Account-level allow/deny overrides can change effective access. A description does not grant additional permissions.
admin-role-purpose-editor = Choose the tasks this administrator needs to perform, then select the corresponding permissions. Read access, exporting data and changing records are separate actions. Review the exact capability identifiers before saving.
admin-role-purpose-selection = These descriptions explain the selected actions. They do not expand the permissions sent to the server.
admin-role-purpose-read = View information in this area.
admin-role-purpose-export = Export information from this area.
admin-role-purpose-revoke = Revoke the sessions or credentials named by this permission.
admin-role-purpose-delete = Delete records covered by this permission.
admin-role-purpose-disable = Disable the accounts covered by this permission.
admin-role-purpose-create = Create records covered by this permission.
admin-role-purpose-specific = Perform the specific action named by this capability; review its identifier before granting it.
admin-role-purpose-description = Purpose and responsibilities
admin-role-purpose-description-help = Explain who should receive this custom role and the tasks they handle (up to 1024 characters). This text does not change its permissions.
